1016	REG_BENGALI_0001	Jain Radhaballabhi with Hing Aar Alur Dom	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Grind urad dal with green chillies, saunf, and generous hing; sauté paste in oil till dry. 2. Stuff spiced dal inside maida dough balls, roll gently and deep fry puffed Luchis. 3. Cook baby potatoes in tomato, hing, and cumin gravy without onion or garlic.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1017	REG_BENGALI_0002	Koraishutir Kochuri	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Grind fresh green peas with green chillies into a smooth paste. 2. Sauté paste in oil with hing, cumin, mouri powder, and salt until moisture dries up into a tight filling. 3. Stuff inside flour dough, roll into discs, and deep fry until golden crisp.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
1018	REG_BENGALI_0003	Mughlai Paratha	Breakfast	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Roll maida dough into a thin large square sheet. 2. Beat eggs with chopped onions, green chillies, coriander, spices, and pre-cooked minced meat. 3. Pour egg mixture in center of dough sheet, fold edges to seal like an envelope, and shallow fry on medium heat till golden crisp.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Non-Vegetarian
1019	REG_BENGALI_0004	Shukto	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Fry Karela and Bori separately in mustard oil. 2. Temper oil with Panch phoron and Radhuni. Add vegetables and sauté briefly. 3. Add water, mustard-poppy paste, and simmer till vegetables cook. Finish with crushed radhuni and mustard oil.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
1020	REG_BENGALI_0005	Jain Shukto	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Fry karela and bori in ghee. 2. Temper ghee with mustard seeds and radhuni. Sauté non-root vegetables (raw banana, papaya, karela, drumsticks). 3. Add poppy seed paste, water, and splash of milk; simmer till soft. Ghee finish.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1022	REG_BENGALI_0007	Shorshe Ilish (Hilsa in Mustard Sauce)	Snack	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Marinate Ilish steaks with turmeric, salt, and mustard oil. 2. Mix yellow mustard, black mustard, and poppy seeds paste with water, turmeric, and green chillies. 3. Heat mustard oil, temper nigella seeds and green chillies, add mustard gravy and fish; simmer gently for 8-10 minutes.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Non-Vegetarian
1023	REG_BENGALI_0008	Chingri Malaikari	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Clean prawns and lightly fry in mustard oil. 2. Temper ghee and oil with whole cinnamon, cardamom, cloves. Add onion, ginger-garlic paste and sauté until golden. 3. Add spices, coconut milk, fried prawns, and simmer till thick creamy sauce forms.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Non-Vegetarian
1024	REG_BENGALI_0009	Telebhaja (Beguni & Chop)	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Slice brinjal lengthwise thinly; sprinkle salt and turmeric. 2. Prepare thick besan batter with kalo jeere, red chilli powder, baking soda, and cold water. 3. Dip brinjal slices in batter and deep fry in hot mustard oil until puffed and crispy.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
1025	REG_BENGALI_0010	Jain Moong Dal Dhokla / Bora	Breakfast	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Coarsely grind soaked moong dal with green chillies. 2. Whisk paste vigorously with hing, cumin seeds, and salt. 3. Drop small lemon-sized balls into hot mustard oil and deep fry on medium heat till golden crisp.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1026	REG_BENGALI_0011	Jhalmuri	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. In a large tin/bowl, combine muri, peanuts, boiled potato, onions, chillies, chanachur, and coriander. 2. Sprinkle muri masala powder, lemon juice, and a generous splash of pungent raw mustard oil. 3. Toss vigorously and serve instantly in paper cones.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
1028	REG_BENGALI_0013	Kosha Mangsho	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Marinate mutton in curd, papaya paste, mustard oil, and spices for 2 hours. 2. Caramelize sugar in mustard oil for dark color, add whole spices and onions; brown deeply. 3. Add ginger-garlic paste, marinated mutton, and slow 'kosha' (sauté continuously) for 1.5 hours on low heat till dark, rich, and oil separates.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Non-Vegetarian
1030	REG_BENGALI_0015	Jain Chonar Dal	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Boil chana dal until tender. 2. Heat ghee, temper bay leaf, cumin, cinnamon, cardamom, and generous hing (no ginger or root crops). 3. Add cooked dal, roasted coconut pieces, raisins, and sugar. Simmer till sweet-savory thick gravy forms.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1032	REG_BENGALI_0017	Jain Chanar Dalna (Without Potatoes)	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Knead fresh chana with a spoonful of maida and salt; press onto tray, cut into diamond shapes, and light-fry in ghee. 2. Heat ghee, add cumin seeds and hing. Add tomato puree and dry spices, sauté until oil leaves sides. 3. Add water, boil, toss in fried chana cubes, and simmer for 5 minutes.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1033	REG_BENGALI_0018	Rosogolla	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Knead fresh chana smoothly until non-greasy; roll into small crack-free smooth balls. 2. Boil thin sugar syrup (1:4 sugar to water ratio) in a wide pot. 3. Drop chana balls into boiling syrup, cover with lid, and boil vigorously for 15 minutes until spongy and doubled in size.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1034	REG_BENGALI_0019	Mishti Doi	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Boil milk and reduce to 3/4th volume. 2. Melt sugar in a separate pan until it turns golden caramel, then pour into hot milk to give reddish-brown color. 3. Cool milk to lukewarm, stir in yogurt culture, pour into earthen clay pots, cover, and leave undisturbed in a warm spot to set overnight.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1035	REG_BENGALI_0020	Sondesh (Nolen Gur Sondesh)	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Knead fresh soft chana smooth. 2. Cook chana and molten Nolen Gur in a non-stick pan over very low heat for 6-8 minutes without letting it dry out. 3. Remove, cool slightly, press into wooden molds (Sanch), unmold, and garnish with pistachios.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1036	REG_BENGALI_0021	Payesh (Chaler Payesh)	Lunch/Dinner	Bengali	Medium	30	1. Wash Gobindobhog rice and smear with ghee. 2. Boil milk with bay leaf and cardamom; reduce slightly. 3. Add rice and slow cook till soft and milk thickens. Add sugar/jaggery, cashews, and raisins; simmer for 5 minutes.	bengali_foods.csv	\N	Jain
