1051	REG_CHINESE_0014	General Tso's Tofu	Lunch/Dinner	Chinese	Medium	30	1. Press tofu, cube, toss in cornstarch, and bake or deep fry till extra crispy. 2. Whisk soy sauce, hoisin sauce, rice vinegar, sugar, cornstarch, and water. 3. Sauté garlic, ginger, dried chillies, pour sauce, toss crispy tofu and steamed broccoli until glazed.	chinese_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
1052	REG_CHINESE_0015	Peking Duck with Pancakes	Breakfast	Chinese	Medium	30	1. Blanch duck, glaze skin with maltose syrup and five-spice; air-dry overnight. 2. Roast in oven at high temperature until skin is dark mahogany brown and ultra-crispy. 3. Slice crispy skin and tender meat; serve wrapped in warm Mandarin pancakes with cucumber, scallions, and sweet bean sauce.	chinese_foods.csv	\N	Non-Vegetarian
1053	REG_CHINESE_0016	Sesame Balls (Jian Dui)	Lunch/Dinner	Chinese	Medium	30	1. Dissolve brown sugar in hot water, knead into glutinous rice flour to form smooth dough. 2. Stuff dough balls with sweet red bean paste, roll tightly. 3. Dampen balls with water, coat generously in white sesame seeds, and deep fry over medium-low heat while pressing gently until expanded, hollow, and golden brown.	chinese_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1054	REG_CHINESE_0017	Mango Sago Pudding	Snack	Chinese	Medium	30	1. Boil small tapioca pearls until transparent, drain, and plunge into ice water. 2. Puree ripe mangoes with coconut milk and sugar until smooth. 3. Combine chilled mango puree, tapioca pearls, diced fresh mangoes, and top with pomelo sacs.	chinese_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
1055	REG_CHINESE_0018	Chinese Date / Red Bean Pancakes	Breakfast	Chinese	Medium	30	1. Knead flour and warm water into soft dough; roll out thin rectangular sheets. 2. Spread red bean paste evenly over half sheet, fold, seal edges, and coat exterior with sesame seeds. 3. Pan-fry in oil/ghee on medium heat until golden brown and flaky.	chinese_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1056	REG_CHINESE_0019	Almond Jelly (Annin Tofu)	Snack	Chinese	Medium	30	1. Dissolve agar-agar powder and sugar in boiling almond milk and soy milk. 2. Stir in almond extract, pour into a shallow dish, and chill in refrigerator until firm set. 3. Cut jelly into diamond cubes, serve chilled submerged in light sugar syrup garnished with mandarin oranges and cherries.	chinese_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
1057	REG_GUJARATI_0000	Khaman Dhokla	Breakfast	Gujarati	Medium	30	1. Whisk besan, sooji, water, sugar, salt, and citric acid into a smooth batter; stir in fruit salt and immediately steam in a greased plate for 15 minutes. 2. Cut steamed fluffy khaman into squares. 3. Prepare tempering in oil with mustard seeds, sesame seeds, green chillies, curry leaves, and hing. Add a splash of sweetened water to tempering and pour over khaman.	gujarati_kathiyawadi_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
