1229	REG_SOUTH_INDIAN_0019	Elaneer Payasam (Tender Coconut Kheer)	Snack	South Indian	Medium	30	1. Blend half the tender coconut pulp into a smooth paste and chop remaining into small bites. 2. Boil milk with condensed milk until slightly reduced; cool completely. 3. Fold in coconut paste, tender coconut bites, coconut water, cardamom, and roasted cashews. Chill before serving.	south_indian_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1230	REG_SOUTH_INDIAN_0020	Double Ka Meetha	Lunch/Dinner	South Indian	Medium	30	1. Deep fry bread triangles in desi ghee till golden brown and crisp. 2. Reduce milk with khoya, sugar, cardamom, and saffron into Rabri. 3. Arrange fried bread in a baking dish, pour hot rabri over it till absorbed, garnish with nuts, and bake briefly.	south_indian_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1231	REG_SOUTH_INDIAN_0021	Payasam (PADA / Ada Pradhaman)	Lunch/Dinner	South Indian	Medium	30	1. Boil rice ada until soft and drain. 2. Melt jaggery and cook soft ada in jaggery syrup till thick. 3. Add thin coconut milk and simmer, then turn off heat and stir in thick coconut milk, cardamom, dry ginger, and fried coconut bites.	south_indian_foods.csv	\N	Vegan
