1112	REG_JAPANESE_0012	Vegetable & Tofu Teriyaki with Rice	Lunch/Dinner	Japanese	Medium	30	1. Press and cube firm tofu; coat in cornstarch and pan-fry in oil until golden crisp. 2. Sauté broccoli, bell peppers, and snow peas in wok. 3. Whisk soy sauce, mirin, sake, and sugar; simmer until glossy thick Teriyaki glaze forms. Toss tofu and veggies in glaze and serve over steamed rice.	japanese_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1116	REG_JAPANESE_0016	Matcha Green Tea Parfait	Snack	Japanese	Medium	30	1. Layer bottom of tall glass with crunchy cornflakes or cake cubes. 2. Pipe vanilla cream, add a scoop of rich matcha ice cream and sweet red bean paste (anko). 3. Top with chewy shiratama dango rice balls and dust with pure ceremonial matcha powder.	japanese_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1120	REG_MAHARASHTRIAN_0000	Kanda Poha	Breakfast	Maharashtrian	Medium	30	1. Rinse poha and drain. 2. Heat oil, fry peanuts, add mustard seeds, green chillies, curry leaves, and chopped onions. Sauté until translucent. 3. Add turmeric and salt, then fold in poha. Cover and steam for 2 minutes. Garnish with lemon juice, coriander, and fresh coconut.	maharashtrian_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1130	REG_MAHARASHTRIAN_0010	Vada Pav	Snack	Maharashtrian	Medium	30	1. Sauté mustard, curry leaves, crushed garlic-chillies, turmeric; mix into mashed potatoes. 2. Roll into balls, dip in spiced besan batter, deep fry until crisp. 3. Serve inside pav smeared with spicy red garlic chutney and green chilli.	maharashtrian_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1146	REG_MEXICAN_0004	Vegetarian Burrito Bowl	Lunch/Dinner	Mexican	Medium	30	1. Cook rice with lime juice and chopped cilantro. Sauté sliced bell peppers and onions with fajita seasoning. 2. Layer bowl with cilantro lime rice, seasoned black beans, and fajita veggies. 3. Top with freshly mashed guacamole, pico de gallo, cheese, and sour cream.	mexican_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1152	REG_MEXICAN_0010	Cheese Quesadilla	Lunch/Dinner	Mexican	Medium	30	1. Heat butter in a skillet over medium heat, place flour tortilla. 2. Generously cover half of tortilla with shredded cheese, fold in half into a half-moon. 3. Cook until tortilla is golden crisp on both sides and cheese is gooey melted. Serve with salsa and sour cream.	mexican_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1154	REG_MEXICAN_0012	Vegetarian Mole Poblano with Mexican Rice	Lunch/Dinner	Mexican	Medium	30	1. Toast dried chillies, nuts, seeds, spices, plantain, and blend with vegetable broth into a complex paste. 2. Simmer sauce in oil and melt in Mexican dark chocolate to create velvety Mole sauce. 3. Toss roasted vegetables/tofu in Mole sauce and serve with tomato-flavored Mexican rice.	mexican_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1162	REG_PUNJABI_0000	Aloo Paratha with White Butter	Breakfast	Punjabi	Medium	30	1. Mash boiled potatoes with onions, green chillies, ginger, amchur, garam masala, and salt. 2. Stuff spiced potato mixture inside whole wheat dough ball, roll into flat circle. 3. Roast on tawa with desi ghee till golden brown. Serve hot with a dollop of fresh white butter and curd.	punjabi_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1172	REG_PUNJABI_0010	Amritsari Kulcha with Chole	Lunch/Dinner	Punjabi	Medium	30	1. Prepare leavened maida dough with curd and baking powder. 2. Stuff dough with mashed potato, onion, crushed anardana, and spices; roll thick. 3. Bake in tandoor or tawa with water splash, crush lightly, and drench in melted butter. Serve with spicy chole.	punjabi_foods.csv	\N	Vegetarian
1180	REG_PUNJABI_0018	Phirni	Lunch/Dinner	Punjabi	Medium	30	1. Boil milk and slowly whisk in coarsely ground rice paste to avoid lumps. 2. Cook on low flame stirring continuously until thick and creamy. 3. Add sugar, saffron milk, and cardamom. Set in clay bowls (Matkas) and chill before serving.	punjabi_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1181	REG_PUNJABI_0019	Gulab Jamun	Snack	Punjabi	Medium	30	1. Knead khoya, paneer, and maida into a smooth soft dough; roll into crack-free balls. 2. Deep fry in ghee on low heat until dark golden brown. 3. Soak immediately in warm saffron-cardamom sugar syrup for at least 2 hours.	punjabi_foods.csv	\N	Jain
1182	REG_PUNJABI_0020	Jalebi with Rabri	Snack	Punjabi	Medium	30	1. Prepare fermented maida batter, pipe spiral shapes into hot ghee, fry until crispy, and soak in saffron sugar syrup. 2. Reduce milk continuously to make thick Rabri. Serve hot crisp jalebis topped with chilled thick rabri.	punjabi_foods.csv	\N	Jain
